  "description": "Talk about the weather, seasons, and daily conditions in Korean.",
  "guidebook": "### Talking About the Weather\n\nIn Korean, talking about precipitation is easy! Instead of saying 'it rains,' Koreans say that rain or snow 'comes':\n- **비가 와요** (*Biga wayo*) = It is raining (literally, 'rain comes').\n- **눈이 와요** (*Nuni wayo*) = It is snowing ('snow comes').\n\n### ㅂ-Irregular Adjectives\nWeather adjectives like **덥다** (*deopda*, to be hot) and **춥다** (*chupda*, to be cold) are irregular. When conjugated into the polite present tense, the **ㅂ** changes to **우**, resulting in:\n- 덥다 → **더워요** (*deowoyo*)\n- 춥다 → **추워요** (*chuwoyo*)\n\n### Seasons with Time Particle -에\nAdd the time particle **-에** (*-e*) to seasons to mean 'in': **여름에** (*in summer*), **겨울에** (*in winter*).",
